Question: Which technical parameters define a harmonised balancing energy bid, for instance how quickly the resource must reach full output?

Answer: Under Commission Regulation (EU) 2017/2195 (the Electricity Balancing Guideline), a harmonised balancing energy bid (referred to as a **standard product**) is defined by a specific set of technical and commercial characteristics. These are outlined in Article 25, with key terms defined in Article 2 (consolidated version of 2022-06-19) [`reg_2017_2195_art25`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619), [`reg_2017_2195_art2`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).

The technical parameters that define a standard balancing energy bid include:

**1. Time-based activation and delivery parameters (addressing your example on response speed):**
* **Preparation period:** The time between the TSO's activation request and the start of the ramping period [`reg_2017_2195_art2`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).
* **Ramping period:** The timeframe during which the resource ramps up or down to meet the requested change [`reg_2017_2195_art25`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).
* **Full activation time:** The total period between the activation request and the corresponding **full delivery** of the product. This directly dictates how quickly a resource must reach its full output [`reg_2017_2195_art2`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).
* **Deactivation period:** The time required to ramp from full delivery back to a set point [`reg_2017_2195_art2`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).
* **Minimum and maximum duration of delivery period:** The timeframe during which the balancing service provider delivers the full requested change of power [`reg_2017_2195_art2`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).
* **Validity period:** The window during which the bid can be activated, defined by a start and end time [`reg_2017_2195_art2`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).
* **Mode of activation:** Whether the bid is triggered manually by an operator or automatically in a closed-loop manner [`reg_2017_2195_art2`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).

**2. Volume and operational parameters:**
* **Minimum and maximum quantity:** The power volume limits of the bid [`reg_2017_2195_art25`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).
* **Divisibility:** Whether the TSO can use only part of the bid (in terms of power or time) [`reg_2017_2195_art2`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).
* **Location:** The defined grid location for the product [`reg_2017_2195_art25`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).
* **Minimum duration between deactivation and following activation:** The mandatory cooldown or reset time required after a delivery ends before the resource can be activated again [`reg_2017_2195_art25`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).

**3. Commercial parameter:**
* **Price of the bid:** The marginal price offered by the balancing service provider [`reg_2017_2195_art25`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).

These parameters are harmonised at the Union level to ensure cross-border competition, liquidity, and technological neutrality in the European balancing markets [`reg_2017_2195_art25`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).

