Question: Can a balancing service provider still update its balancing energy bid after gate closure?

Answer: No, a balancing service provider cannot update its balancing energy bid after the gate closure time. 

According to **Commission Regulation (EU) 2017/2195** (consolidated version of 2022-06-19), the *balancing energy gate closure time* is explicitly defined as the point in time when the submission or update of a balancing energy bid for a standard product is no longer permitted [`reg_2017_2195_art2`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619). Article 24(3) reinforces this by stating that after the gate closure time, balancing service providers `"shall no longer be permitted to submit or update their balancing energy bids"` [`reg_2017_2195_art24`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).

However, after the gate closure time, balancing service providers are still required to report any **unavailable volumes** of their balancing energy bids to the connecting TSO without undue delay [`reg_2017_2195_art24`](https://publications.europa.eu/resource/celex/02017R2195-20220619).

